@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.762 = private unnamed_addr constant [586 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `trio.sleep()` or `anyio.sleep()` with a delay greater than 24 hours.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACalling `sleep()` with a delay greater than 24 hours is usually intended\0Ato sleep indefinitely. Instead of using a large delay,\0A`trio.sleep_forever()` or `anyio.sleep_forever()` better conveys the intent.\0A\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport trio\0A\0A\0Aasync def func():\0A    await trio.sleep(86401)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport trio\0A\0A\0Aasync def func():\0A    await trio.sleep_forever()\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AThis fix is marked as unsafe as it changes program behavior.\0A", align 1
