@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.772 = private unnamed_addr constant [661 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for potential uses of hardcoded passwords in function calls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIncluding a hardcoded password in source code is a security risk, as an\0Aattacker could discover the password and use it to gain unauthorized\0Aaccess.\0A\0AInstead, store passwords and other secrets in configuration files,\0Aenvironment variables, or other sources that are excluded from version\0Acontrol.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aconnect_to_server(password=\22hunter2\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0Aconnect_to_server(password=os.environ[\22PASSWORD\22])\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-259](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/259.html)\0A", align 1
