@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.809 = private unnamed_addr constant [29 x i8] c"duplicate-try-block-exception", align 1
@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.810 = private unnamed_addr constant [522 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `try-except` blocks with duplicate exception handlers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADuplicate exception handlers are redundant, as the first handler will catch\0Athe exception, making the second handler unreachable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A", align 1
