@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.868 = private unnamed_addr constant [1317 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function arguments that use the same names as builtins.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AReusing a builtin name for the name of an argument increases the\0Adifficulty of reading and maintaining the code, and can cause\0Anon-obvious errors, as readers may mistake the argument for the\0Abuiltin and vice versa.\0A\0ABuiltins can be marked as exceptions to this rule via the\0A[`lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef remove_duplicates(list, list2):\0A    result = set()\0A    for value in list:\0A        result.add(value)\0A    for value in list2:\0A        result.add(value)\0A    return list(result)  # TypeError: 'list' object is not callable\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef remove_duplicates(list1, list2):\0A    result = set()\0A    for value in list1:\0A        result.add(value)\0A    for value in list2:\0A        result.add(value)\0A    return list(result)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`\0A\0A## References\0A- [_Is it bad practice to use a built-in function name as an attribute or method identifier?_](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/9109333/is-it-bad-practice-to-use-a-built-in-function-name-as-an-attribute-or-method-ide)\0A- [_Why is it a bad idea to name a variable `id` in Python?_](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77552/id-is-a-bad-variable-name-in-python)\0A", align 1
