@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.902 = private unnamed_addr constant [570 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for logging calls with `exc_info=` outside exception handlers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing `exc_info=True` outside of an exception handler\0Aattaches `None` as the exception information, leading to confusing messages:\0A\0A```pycon\0A>>> logging.warning(\22Uh oh\22, exc_info=True)\0AWARNING:root:Uh oh\0ANoneType: None\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0A\0Alogging.warning(\22Foobar\22, exc_info=True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0A\0Alogging.warning(\22Foobar\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix is always marked as unsafe, as it changes runtime behavior.\0A", align 1
