@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.906 = private unnamed_addr constant [741 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `.exception()` logging calls outside of exception handlers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[The documentation] states:\0A> This function should only be called from an exception handler.\0A\0ACalling `.exception()` outside of an exception handler\0Aattaches `None` as exception information, leading to confusing messages:\0A\0A```pycon\0A>>> logging.exception(\22example\22)\0AERROR:root:example\0ANoneType: None\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.exception(\22Foobar\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.error(\22Foobar\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix, if available, will always be marked as unsafe, as it changes runtime behavior.\0A\0A[The documentation]: https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.html#logging.exception\0A", align 1
