@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.933 = private unnamed_addr constant [1065 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for classes inheriting from `typing.Generic[]` where `Generic[]` is\0Anot the last base class in the bases tuple.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf `Generic[]` is not the final class in the bases tuple, unexpected\0Abehaviour can occur at runtime (See [this CPython issue][1] for an example).\0AThe rule is also applied to stub files, but, unlike at runtime,\0Ain stubs it is purely enforced for stylistic consistency.\0A\0AFor example:\0A```python\0Aclass LinkedList(Generic[T], Sized):\0A    def push(self, item: T) -> None:\0A        self._items.append(item)\0A\0Aclass MyMapping(\0A    Generic[K, V],\0A    Iterable[Tuple[K, V]],\0A    Container[Tuple[K, V]],\0A):\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass LinkedList(Sized, Generic[T]):\0A    def push(self, item: T) -> None:\0A        self._items.append(item)\0A\0Aclass MyMapping(\0A    Iterable[Tuple[K, V]],\0A    Container[Tuple[K, V]],\0A    Generic[K, V],\0A):\0A    ...\0A```\0A## References\0A- [`typing.Generic` documentation](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Generic)\0A\0A[1]: https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/106102\0A", align 1
