@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.952 = private unnamed_addr constant [736 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of string and bytes literals longer than 50 characters\0Ain stub (`.pyi`) files.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a function or variable has a default value where the string or bytes\0Arepresentation is greater than 50 characters long, it is likely to be an\0Aimplementation detail or a constant that varies depending on the system\0Ayou're running on.\0A\0AAlthough IDEs may find them useful, default values are ignored by type\0Acheckers, the primary consumers of stub files. Replace very long constants\0Awith ellipses (`...`) to simplify the stub.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: str = \2251 character stringgggggggggggggggggggggggggggggggg\22) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: str = ...) -> None: ...\0A```\0A", align 1
