@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.971 = private unnamed_addr constant [718 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for use of `zip()` to iterate over keys and values of a dictionary at once.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `dict` type provides an `.items()` method which is faster and more readable.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aflag_stars = {\22USA\22: 50, \22Slovenia\22: 3, \22Panama\22: 2, \22Australia\22: 6}\0A\0Afor country, stars in zip(flag_stars.keys(), flag_stars.values()):\0A    print(f\22{country}'s flag has {stars} stars.\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aflag_stars = {\22USA\22: 50, \22Slovenia\22: 3, \22Panama\22: 2, \22Australia\22: 6}\0A\0Afor country, stars in flag_stars.items():\0A    print(f\22{country}'s flag has {stars} stars.\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `dict.items`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#dict.items)\0A", align 1
