@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1080 = private unnamed_addr constant [615 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `nonlocal` names without bindings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`nonlocal` names must be bound to a name in an outer scope.\0AViolating this rule leads to a `SyntaxError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    def get_bar(self):\0A        nonlocal bar\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    bar = 1\0A\0A    def get_bar(self):\0A        nonlocal bar\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `nonlocal` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#nonlocal)\0A- [PEP 3104 \E2\80\93 Access to Names in Outer Scopes](https://peps.python.org/pep-3104/)\0A", align 1
