@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1094 = private unnamed_addr constant [611 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for non-method functions decorated with `@singledispatchmethod`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `@singledispatchmethod` decorator is intended for use with methods, not\0Afunctions.\0A\0AInstead, use the `@singledispatch` decorator.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom functools import singledispatchmethod\0A\0A\0A@singledispatchmethod\0Adef func(arg): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom functools import singledispatch\0A\0A\0A@singledispatch\0Adef func(arg): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as migrating from `@singledispatchmethod` to\0A`@singledispatch` may change the behavior of the code.\0A", align 1
