@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1114 = private unnamed_addr constant [642 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for an exception that is not raised.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to create an exception without raising it. For example,\0A`ValueError(\22...\22)` on its own will have no effect (unlike\0A`raise ValueError(\22...\22)`) and is likely a mistake.\0A\0A## Known problems\0AThis rule only detects built-in exceptions, like `ValueError`, and does\0Anot catch user-defined exceptions.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0AValueError(\22...\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Araise ValueError(\22...\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as converting a useless exception\0Astatement to a `raise` statement will change the program's behavior.\0A", align 1
