@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1154 = private unnamed_addr constant [729 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of `IOBase.write` in a for loop.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen writing a batch of elements, it's more idiomatic to use a single method call to\0A`IOBase.writelines`, rather than write elements one by one.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Awith Path(\22file\22).open(\22w\22) as f:\0A    for line in lines:\0A        f.write(line)\0A\0Awith Path(\22file\22).open(\22wb\22) as f:\0A    for line in lines:\0A        f.write(line.encode())\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Awith Path(\22file\22).open(\22w\22) as f:\0A    f.writelines(lines)\0A\0Awith Path(\22file\22).open(\22wb\22) as f:\0A    f.writelines(line.encode() for line in lines)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `io.IOBase.writelines`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/io.html#io.IOBase.writelines)\0A", align 1
