@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1161 = private unnamed_addr constant [834 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `isinstance` that check if an object is of type `None`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThere is only ever one instance of `None`, so it is more efficient and\0Areadable to use the `is` operator to check if an object is `None`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aisinstance(obj, type(None))\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aobj is None\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix will be marked as unsafe if there are any comments within the call.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `isinstance`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#isinstance)\0A- [Python documentation: `None`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/constants.html#None)\0A- [Python documentation: `type`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#type)\0A- [Python documentation: Identity comparisons](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#is-not)\0A", align 1
