@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1164 = private unnamed_addr constant [18 x i8] c"print-empty-string", align 1
@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1165 = private unnamed_addr constant [640 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `print` calls with unnecessary empty strings as positional\0Aarguments and unnecessary `sep` keyword arguments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APrefer calling `print` without any positional arguments, which is\0Aequivalent and more concise.\0A\0ASimilarly, when printing one or fewer items, the `sep` keyword argument,\0A(used to define the string that separates the `print` arguments) can be\0Aomitted, as it's redundant when there are no items to separate.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aprint(\22\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aprint()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `print`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#print)\0A", align 1
