@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1171 = private unnamed_addr constant [792 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `open` and `read` that can be replaced by `pathlib`\0Amethods, like `Path.read_text` and `Path.read_bytes`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen reading the entire contents of a file into a variable, it's simpler\0Aand more concise to use `pathlib` methods like `Path.read_text` and\0A`Path.read_bytes` instead of `open` and `read` calls via `with` statements.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Awith open(filename) as f:\0A    contents = f.read()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0Acontents = Path(filename).read_text()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.read_bytes`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path.read_bytes)\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.read_text`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path.read_text)\0A", align 1
