@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1178 = private unnamed_addr constant [523 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of shorthand aliases for regular expression flags\0A(e.g., `re.I` instead of `re.IGNORECASE`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe regular expression module provides descriptive names for each flag,\0Aalong with single-letter aliases. Prefer the descriptive names, as they\0Aare more readable and self-documenting.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport re\0A\0Aif re.match(\22^hello\22, \22hello world\22, re.I):\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport re\0A\0Aif re.match(\22^hello\22, \22hello world\22, re.IGNORECASE):\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A", align 1
