@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1202 = private unnamed_addr constant [783 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `open` and `write` that can be replaced by `pathlib`\0Amethods, like `Path.write_text` and `Path.write_bytes`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen writing a single string to a file, it's simpler and more concise\0Ato use `pathlib` methods like `Path.write_text` and `Path.write_bytes`\0Ainstead of `open` and `write` calls via `with` statements.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Awith open(filename, \22w\22) as f:\0A    f.write(contents)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom pathlib import Path\0A\0APath(filename).write_text(contents)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.write_bytes`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path.write_bytes)\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.write_text`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path.write_text)\0A", align 1
