@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1245 = private unnamed_addr constant [488 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for excessive logging of exception objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen logging exceptions via `logging.exception`, the exception object\0Ais logged automatically. Including the exception object in the log\0Amessage is redundant and can lead to excessive logging.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError as e:\0A    logger.exception(f\22Found an error: {e}\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError:\0A    logger.exception(\22Found an error\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
